**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests`
- `unit-tests`: `BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests`, `BerremanTests.DispersionFormulaTests`

**How to implement.** The Tauc-Lorentz and Gaussian-oscillator models become axis data, evaluated by kernels that MOVE into the core, so one implementation exists (.spec-md §3.1). (1) `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`: (a) `AbscissaKind` gains `member abscissaAt (w : WaveLength) : float`: `LinearInX scale` answers `w.value / scale`, and `ReciprocalInX r` answers `r.numerator / (w.value / r.wavelengthScale)`. For every `UnitOfMeasure` this is the same floating-point arithmetic as `fromMeters` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/Units.fs:104-114`) over the scale and numerator `ofUnit` derives, so the abscissa is bit-identical. (b) Two records marked `[<Softellect.Sys.NumericCarrier("...")>]`: `TaucLorentzLaw` (`epsInf`, `amplitude`, `resonance`, `broadening`, `bandGap`, `abscissa : AbscissaKind`) and `GaussianOscillatorLaw` (`epsInf`, `amplitude`, `energy`, `broadening`, `abscissa : AbscissaKind`). Each has `member complexIndex (w : WaveLength) : ComplexRefractionIndex`, whose body is its arm of `baseIndex` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:508-517`) moved verbatim over `x = this.abscissa.abscissaAt w`. (c) `EpsAxisDispersion` gains `TaucLorentzAxis of TaucLorentzLaw` and `GaussianOscillatorAxis of GaussianOscillatorLaw`. `complexIndex` calls the law, and the custom `Equals` / `GetHashCode` compare and hash both structurally. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs`: `TaucLorentzCoefficients` and `GaussianOscillatorCoefficients` gain `member toTaucLorentzLaw : TaucLorentzLaw` and `member toGaussianOscillatorLaw : GaussianOscillatorLaw`. Each copies the coefficients and takes `abscissa = AbscissaKind.ofUnit this.wavelengthUnit`. `thermoOptic` is not carried, because lowering stays isothermal: `evaluateAt` (`:552-559`) still adds the correction on top of `baseIndex`. `baseIndex`'s two arms answer the law's index, and their bodies are deleted there. `toEpsAxis` (`:766-769`) lowers `TaucLorentz c` to `TaucLorentzAxis c.toTaucLorentzLaw` and `GaussianOscillator c` to `GaussianOscillatorAxis c.toGaussianOscillatorLaw`; `ForouhiBloomer` and `BrendelBormann` still lower to the evaluated case until step 7. `parameters`' `SumOfTerms` arm (`:427-435`) answers `[]` for both new cases. The doc comments of `baseIndex`, `toEpsAxis`, `toEpsValue` and `toOpticalProperties` (`:485-489`, `:669-686`, `:763-765`, `:793-812`) say that these two models lower to their law. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs` `facetKey` (`:91-95`) maps both new cases to the existing `DiscreteKey "Evaluated (transcendental)"`, so `every DispersionModel kind lands on the vocabulary key its lowering denotes` (`OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs:464-482`) stays green unchanged. `MaterialComplexity.isEditable` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:864-871`) treats both as data that is not editable term data, as today. (4) Facts. `Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs` gains `The Tauc-Lorentz law reproduces its reference index on both sides of the band gap`, `The Tauc-Lorentz law over a micrometre abscissa reproduces its reference index` and `The Gaussian-oscillator law reproduces its reference index`. They build the laws directly in the core. The first and third use the Tauc-Lorentz and Gaussian sets of `DispersionModelsTests.fs:306-326` over the electron-volt abscissa `ReciprocalInX { wavelengthScale = 1.0e-9<meter>; numerator = 1239.84 }`. The second uses a Tauc-Lorentz set over `LinearInX 1.0e-6<meter>` whose band gap lies between 0.3 µm and 2.0 µm. Each compares `complexIndex` at 300, 450, 600, 900 and 2000 nm, with exact `Assert.Equal`, against G17 literals the worker records from the start tree's `DispersionModel.evaluate` before moving the arms. In `DispersionModelsTests.fs`, `AC-B5 transcendental models lower to the evaluated case and match evaluate` (`:300-337`) matches each model's own law case where it matched `EpsAxisEvaluated _`, and `AC-B5 toEpsValue short-circuits ConstantNK and builds a single-segment tree otherwise` (`:380-382`) matches `TaucLorentzAxis _`. Their exact `Assert.Equal((f w).value, (axis.complexIndex w).value)` and 1e-12 assertions are unchanged, and their comments (`:302-305`, `:378-379`) no longer name `EpsAxisEvaluated`.

**Acceptance.** After the two laws land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `equal Tauc-Lorentz and Gaussian-oscillator models lower to equal axis data` (red since step 4), with DispersionModelsTests' AC-B6 reference facts and LibraryFacetsTests unchanged; unit-tests (EpsWithDispValueTests, DispersionFormulaTests) MUST pass, with the three new law facts equal to their literals; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.
